{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\eng\\078.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "9. Gently make small circles or up and down movements on the teeth surfaces with the", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[100, 213], [1190, 213], [1190, 249], [100, 249]]}, {"text": "bristles, moving all over the mouth, for at least 2 minutes.", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[146, 252], [859, 256], [858, 288], [146, 284]]}, {"text": " 10. Remember that it's important to also clean the gums and the tongue as well.", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[96, 289], [1099, 285], [1099, 326], [96, 331]]}, {"text": "11. After 2 minutes of brushing, cautiously spit the leftover paste into the sink.", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[99, 326], [1075, 323], [1075, 366], [99, 368]]}, {"text": "12. Crack a quick, but big smile to check to see if your teeth and mouth are clean.", "conf": 0.942, "box": [[97, 366], [1115, 364], [1115, 404], [97, 406]]}, {"text": "13. Fill your palm with the cold water from the tap and take a sip.", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[102, 406], [906, 408], [906, 441], [102, 439]]}, {"text": "14. Gargle and swish the water around your mouth until all the toothpaste residue has", "conf": 0.945, "box": [[96, 444], [1169, 440], [1170, 480], [96, 484]]}, {"text": "been removed from the teeth.", "conf": 0.854, "box": [[147, 487], [522, 488], [522, 515], [147, 514]]}, {"text": "16. While the water is running, rinse off the toothbrush so it's ready for the next time.", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[93, 560], [1158, 559], [1158, 595], [93, 596]]}, {"text": "17. Now your teeth are clean, germ-free, sparkling, and free of cavities and stink breath.", "conf": 0.935, "box": [[99, 598], [1186, 595], [1186, 635], [99, 638]]}, {"text": " 18. When it's time to smile for a picture, you'll be ready with the most beautiful, white,", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[89, 639], [1168, 636], [1168, 672], [89, 675]]}, {"text": "sparkly, shiny teeth.", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[148, 679], [391, 679], [391, 712], [148, 712]]}, {"text": "2 Find the adjectives for the following nouns. You have to refer back to the", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[98, 798], [1103, 794], [1103, 823], [98, 827]]}, {"text": "passage to find them.", "conf": 0.879, "box": [[136, 837], [423, 832], [423, 862], [136, 867]]}, {"text": "Nouns", "conf": 0.81, "box": [[342, 887], [435, 887], [435, 918], [342, 918]]}, {"text": "Adjectives", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[798, 884], [937, 884], [937, 914], [798, 914]]}, {"text": "teeth", "conf": 0.753, "box": [[340, 936], [413, 936], [413, 968], [340, 968]]}, {"text": "Gleaming,glistening,gleaming", "conf": 0.883, "box": [[681, 932], [1071, 935], [1071, 965], [681, 962]]}, {"text": "mouth", "conf": 0.804, "box": [[339, 986], [428, 986], [428, 1017], [339, 1017]]}, {"text": "gums", "conf": 0.799, "box": [[336, 1042], [414, 1035], [416, 1066], [339, 1073]]}, {"text": "toothbrush", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[337, 1088], [480, 1083], [481, 1114], [339, 1119]]}, {"text": "mirror", "conf": 0.781, "box": [[337, 1138], [422, 1138], [422, 1169], [337, 1169]]}, {"text": "smile", "conf": 0.817, "box": [[336, 1186], [408, 1186], [408, 1218], [336, 1218]]}, {"text": "toothpaste", "conf": 0.813, "box": [[337, 1237], [475, 1237], [475, 1268], [337, 1268]]}, {"text": "Comprehension Questians", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[84, 1284], [494, 1285], [494, 1318], [83, 1317]]}, {"text": "1 Read the passage again and write down the procedure for brushing your teeth in", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[85, 1331], [1211, 1327], [1211, 1366], [86, 1370]]}, {"text": "simple steps.", "conf": 0.89, "box": [[124, 1372], [301, 1376], [301, 1407], [123, 1402]]}, {"text": "2 Why is it important to clean your teeth twice a day? What will happen if you", "conf": 0.916, "box": [[85, 1419], [1153, 1418], [1153, 1454], [85, 1455]]}, {"text": "do not brush them properly?", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[125, 1460], [510, 1460], [510, 1490], [125, 1490]]}, {"text": "However, bristle has a different meaning in the passage. Can you identify the", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[126, 1555], [1164, 1556]